{
 "_meta": {
  "purpose": "Authoritative boundary of what the JUNO-60 (Cloud 60) product actually EXPOSES, vs. shared RolandCloud framework code/params/tables that are compiled into the DLL but unused by this product. Built capture-free from the decompiled binary + factory preset DB + the confirmed panel photo.",
  "method": "Three binary-grounded sources cross-referenced: (1) the parameter registry (sub_388170 -> docs/PARAM_MAP.tsv): 1121 descriptors = one ~110-param framework voice template replicated ~16x (16 parts) \u2014 names like 'LFO Level','ENV Attack' each appear 16x. (2) the factory-preset DB synth block (DB 755..877, refs/default_patch.json): the 123 params the preset format actually stores, each with a value-format SPEC that is the panel's control labelling. (3) the confirmed JUNO-60 panel (ARPEGGIO/ARP MODE/ARP RANGE + the standard DCO/VCF/VCA/ENV/LFO/CHORUS sections).",
  "key_finding": "'Present in the binary' != 'exposed by the product'. The exposed JUNO-60 patch surface is the 123-param DB block, NOT the 1121-param registry. Mapping work must be scoped to the 123, not the 1121 \u2014 the framework superset is what made the DB->engine continuous-param binding look intractable.",
  "uidesc_note": "The definitive panel control->ParamID map lives in the VST3 bundle's Resources/*.uidesc (VSTGUI), which is NOT inside the decompiled PE (only VSTGUI parser error strings + SVG assets are present). So the exact per-control ParamID is confirmable only with the bundle file; the DB block + specs give the exposed SET authoritatively without it."
 },
